How to Access It
Once the spring-boot-app pods are running on EKS, expose the service:


# Check if the service exists
kubectl get svc -n default
If spring-boot-app-service shows as NodePort (from the deployment manifests), expose it via LoadBalancer or port-forward:

Option A: Port-forward (Quick test)

kubectl port-forward svc/spring-boot-app-service -n default 9090:80 --address 0.0.0.0 &
Open port 9090 on EC2 security group, then access:


http://35.166.44.155:9090
